WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:03.580
- I mean, I, I, I'm a person
who does her homework a lot.

00:00:03.580 --> 00:00:04.420
(intense music)

00:00:04.420 --> 00:00:06.260
You already know, my teachers out there.

00:00:06.260 --> 00:00:08.741
But, it's just too much.

00:00:08.741 --> 00:00:12.470
(upbeat jazzy music)

00:00:12.470 --> 00:00:14.280
- Hello, my name is Dylan Jodzik.

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:16.240
I'm 18 years old, I'm
a high school senior.

00:00:16.240 --> 00:00:17.710
- Hi, my name is Rachel.

00:00:17.710 --> 00:00:20.350
I am 18 years old, I'm
a senior in high school

00:00:20.350 --> 00:00:22.710
and today we are going
to react to some TikToks.

00:00:22.710 --> 00:00:23.960
- My teacher, Mr Ferroni,

00:00:23.960 --> 00:00:26.400
actually is a pretty famous TikToker.

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:29.210
- All my free time, like 90%
of the time I'm on TikTok.

00:00:29.210 --> 00:00:31.480
I'm not usually on the teacher side

00:00:31.480 --> 00:00:34.463
'cause I don't wanna find my
teacher, who has a TikTok.

00:00:34.463 --> 00:00:37.100
- My students never
complete all their homework.

00:00:37.100 --> 00:00:38.325
I don't know what to do.

00:00:38.325 --> 00:00:40.490
Why are you assigning so much homework?

00:00:40.490 --> 00:00:43.010
Why are you overloading
these kids with homework?

00:00:43.010 --> 00:00:44.460
Let them rest when they get home.

00:00:44.460 --> 00:00:45.377
Don't you want to take a nap?

00:00:45.377 --> 00:00:47.500
I'm sure they do too.

00:00:47.500 --> 00:00:48.370
- For real!

00:00:48.370 --> 00:00:51.180
Yeah, I have some teachers
that assign so much homework.

00:00:51.180 --> 00:00:52.442
Do they realize, like, we have, like,

00:00:52.442 --> 00:00:54.210
a life outside of school.

00:00:54.210 --> 00:00:57.160
- As a senior, 'senioritis'
is a real disease.

00:00:57.160 --> 00:00:58.300
Already accepted into college,

00:00:58.300 --> 00:00:59.760
why do you guys give me more homework?

00:00:59.760 --> 00:01:01.508
We have jobs, I've got sports.

00:01:01.508 --> 00:01:04.490
There's other stuff in
our life that we wanna do.

00:01:04.490 --> 00:01:05.323
- It's just too much.

00:01:05.323 --> 00:01:07.480
I don't know why you're
assigning homework.

00:01:07.480 --> 00:01:08.980
We do it in class anyways.

00:01:08.980 --> 00:01:10.064
I'll study, I promise.

00:01:10.064 --> 00:01:10.910
(giggles)

00:01:10.910 --> 00:01:12.640
- I can get it, at the
beginning of the year, you know,

00:01:12.640 --> 00:01:15.239
you still have to build
credit and stuff for college.

00:01:15.239 --> 00:01:17.770
But by the end of the
year, like, you know,

00:01:17.770 --> 00:01:19.107
now we're in April, May,

00:01:19.107 --> 00:01:22.520
just, just why even give us homework?

00:01:22.520 --> 00:01:24.100
It's usually like, "Oh, why,
homework's not that hard."

00:01:24.100 --> 00:01:26.570
Yes, it's not that hard,
but I have 10 other classes.

00:01:26.570 --> 00:01:28.625
We're staying home anyway,
like, it's already homework

00:01:28.625 --> 00:01:32.240
even though we're at school, technically.

00:01:32.240 --> 00:01:33.777
- Hey, why were you absent yesterday?

00:01:33.777 --> 00:01:35.169
- [Student] I was at a funeral.

00:01:35.169 --> 00:01:36.883
- Oh, I am so sorry for your loss

00:01:36.883 --> 00:01:38.540
- [Student] It's okay I
didn't really like the man.

00:01:38.540 --> 00:01:40.105
- Oh my gosh.

00:01:40.105 --> 00:01:43.182
(giggling)

00:01:43.182 --> 00:01:45.820
- Aah, that's really funny.

00:01:45.820 --> 00:01:48.540
- I don't know how to comment on that one.

00:01:48.540 --> 00:01:50.187
I've definitely had that
excuse where I was, like,

00:01:50.187 --> 00:01:52.413
"I'm sick" but I'm really not.

00:01:52.413 --> 00:01:53.610
I just wanna sleep in.

00:01:53.610 --> 00:01:55.450
Right now with, like, virtual learning

00:01:55.450 --> 00:01:57.900
I can't really fake being sick

00:01:57.900 --> 00:01:59.770
or I can't really fake being anywhere,

00:01:59.770 --> 00:02:01.100
cause they know I'm at home.

00:02:01.100 --> 00:02:02.920
- I mean, you go to funerals all the time.

00:02:02.920 --> 00:02:05.020
Sometimes for people that you don't know

00:02:05.020 --> 00:02:06.410
and at least the teacher took it well,

00:02:06.410 --> 00:02:08.440
she wasn't mad or anything.

00:02:08.440 --> 00:02:10.680
I'm sure she hears stuff
like that all the time.

00:02:10.680 --> 00:02:12.040
- Good morning students,

00:02:12.040 --> 00:02:13.086
welcome to another day of online class.

00:02:13.086 --> 00:02:14.230
(crosstalk)

00:02:14.230 --> 00:02:16.710
So today we're going to
get back into chapter six.

00:02:16.710 --> 00:02:19.243
Is there going to any
questions about biomathematics?

00:02:20.221 --> 00:02:21.753
- Oh my gosh.

00:02:21.753 --> 00:02:23.330
(laughing)

00:02:23.330 --> 00:02:24.230
- That's my teacher,

00:02:24.230 --> 00:02:25.084
Mr. Feronni.

00:02:25.084 --> 00:02:26.125
- That's my teacher,

00:02:26.125 --> 00:02:26.980
Mr Feronni.

00:02:26.980 --> 00:02:27.830
- I promise you,

00:02:27.830 --> 00:02:29.100
He does not dress like that.

00:02:29.100 --> 00:02:30.550
That's not even the right room he's in,

00:02:30.550 --> 00:02:32.780
he's lying when he makes these tiktoks.

00:02:32.780 --> 00:02:33.680
It's really funny,

00:02:33.680 --> 00:02:35.550
like, when he tries to make tiktoks

00:02:35.550 --> 00:02:37.330
in class and you volunteer to participate

00:02:37.330 --> 00:02:40.560
in it and it was like, he'll
be like 'Okay, that was good.'

00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:43.030
but he'll be lying to you
because he knows it wasn't good.

00:02:43.030 --> 00:02:44.830
But I promise you, Mr. Feronni

00:02:44.830 --> 00:02:46.560
is never wearing shorts

00:02:46.560 --> 00:02:48.490
and he's never wearing a suit jacket,

00:02:48.490 --> 00:02:50.020
but he's always happy to teach us.

00:02:50.020 --> 00:02:51.260
And I'm glad to have him as a teacher.

00:02:51.260 --> 00:02:53.112
- I remember one time in class,

00:02:53.112 --> 00:02:55.623
he was testing to see
who was paying attention.

00:02:55.623 --> 00:02:57.130
He would turn off his camera and be like

00:02:57.130 --> 00:02:58.590
my connection is not
working and he turned it

00:02:58.590 --> 00:03:01.070
on and he has a completely
different shirt on it.

00:03:01.070 --> 00:03:04.010
Ended up being like, he changed
his shirt like 11 times.

00:03:04.010 --> 00:03:06.840
And he was like, nobody noticed it.

00:03:06.840 --> 00:03:08.570
I'm paying attention to the lesson.

00:03:08.570 --> 00:03:09.403
Not what you're wearing.

00:03:09.403 --> 00:03:10.236
(laughing)

00:03:10.236 --> 00:03:11.069
- All right guys.

00:03:11.069 --> 00:03:11.902
That's it for today.

00:03:11.902 --> 00:03:13.420
Just make sure you
complete your assignment.

00:03:13.420 --> 00:03:14.780
It's so great to see you guys.

00:03:14.780 --> 00:03:15.613
Have a great day

00:03:15.613 --> 00:03:16.540
and I'll see you soon.

00:03:24.487 --> 00:03:25.940
- Awh, this one was kind of sad.

00:03:25.940 --> 00:03:28.070
- Yeah. I started to notice

00:03:28.070 --> 00:03:31.350
like there was one time I stayed
behind just to try to talk

00:03:31.350 --> 00:03:33.458
to my teacher about something and

00:03:33.458 --> 00:03:35.610
as like all the cameras are going off.

00:03:35.610 --> 00:03:38.800
I think that teacher thought I left.

00:03:38.800 --> 00:03:43.120
So like I just saw the
teacher like, like 'I'm done.'

00:03:43.120 --> 00:03:45.067
I had to like unmute
myself, 'I'm still here.

00:03:45.067 --> 00:03:46.361
I'm really sorry.'

00:03:46.361 --> 00:03:48.125
And he's like, 'Oh no, no, no, no, no.

00:03:48.125 --> 00:03:50.460
That's fine. I'm okay.'

00:03:50.460 --> 00:03:51.894
But I think I feel you.

00:03:51.894 --> 00:03:53.330
I think I feel the teachers.

00:03:53.330 --> 00:03:56.030
- I know Mr Feronni is
being truthfully honest

00:03:56.030 --> 00:03:59.160
because I've seen the days
when his Chromebooks acting up

00:03:59.160 --> 00:04:02.664
and stuff and he's just
like so upset and so angry.

00:04:02.664 --> 00:04:05.430
And my other teachers too,
like they're not getting what

00:04:05.430 --> 00:04:07.100
they signed up for to be a teacher.

00:04:07.100 --> 00:04:08.990
You know, people got to
think of the teachers too.

00:04:08.990 --> 00:04:11.001
I mean, if you think about it,
this is, this is their life.

00:04:11.001 --> 00:04:11.834
(laughing)

00:04:11.834 --> 00:04:14.440
I've had them in class,
in person and they just

00:04:14.440 --> 00:04:18.356
have so much more energy and
so much more like bedazzle.

00:04:18.356 --> 00:04:19.870
And it's just like,

00:04:19.870 --> 00:04:22.880
you can't convey that over
the screen the same way.

00:04:22.880 --> 00:04:24.890
- Yo, Mr. Feronni..

00:04:24.890 --> 00:04:26.050
- Do I know you?

00:04:26.050 --> 00:04:26.883
- Junior your student

00:04:26.883 --> 00:04:28.510
for the last hundred days?

00:04:28.510 --> 00:04:30.050
- Honestly, doesn't ring a bell.

00:04:30.050 --> 00:04:32.203
- Okay. How about now?

00:04:33.830 --> 00:04:34.663
- Oh my God.

00:04:34.663 --> 00:04:35.496
Junior. What's up?

00:04:36.360 --> 00:04:37.193
- All right.

00:04:37.193 --> 00:04:38.220
That's what I mean when Mr. Feronni

00:04:38.220 --> 00:04:40.100
is always making us do tiktoks.

00:04:40.100 --> 00:04:42.810
I guarantee you that took
them 30 minutes to make.

00:04:42.810 --> 00:04:45.230
I went to hybrid school and half

00:04:45.230 --> 00:04:47.890
of my teachers didn't know who I was.

00:04:47.890 --> 00:04:49.090
You know, I don't blame them

00:04:49.090 --> 00:04:51.723
because I'm not really
good with names myself.

00:04:55.080 --> 00:04:57.530
- I have terrible eyesight.

00:04:57.530 --> 00:04:59.405
I'm going to pause it so I can read it.

00:04:59.405 --> 00:05:01.860
(reading the text on the screen)

00:05:01.860 --> 00:05:03.097
- Yeah, I mean..

00:05:04.500 --> 00:05:05.780
- Yeah, that's crazy.

00:05:05.780 --> 00:05:06.900
It's like when you're a kid

00:05:06.900 --> 00:05:08.750
and you see your teacher
at the grocery store,

00:05:08.750 --> 00:05:12.300
it's like, changes your
whole view on life.

00:05:12.300 --> 00:05:13.250
- As a student,

00:05:13.250 --> 00:05:16.050
if I go to my teacher, I'll
just be like, I will never

00:05:16.050 --> 00:05:19.470
see you other than who
you are in front of me.

00:05:19.470 --> 00:05:22.330
If you tell me you like the
same music as me, like cool.

00:05:22.330 --> 00:05:25.390
But also that's weird

00:05:25.390 --> 00:05:26.223
- I'm going to give these out in

00:05:26.223 --> 00:05:28.610
every class in case I
start talking too much.

00:05:28.610 --> 00:05:29.475
It's only fair.

00:05:29.475 --> 00:05:30.308
All right.

00:05:30.308 --> 00:05:31.141
So I'll give it out and you give it

00:05:31.141 --> 00:05:32.600
to me and tell me you
think I'm talking too much.

00:05:32.600 --> 00:05:33.560
We'll start with junior,

00:05:33.560 --> 00:05:34.393
So here you go.

00:05:34.393 --> 00:05:37.210
Give it to me anytime I'm
talking to much all right?

00:05:37.210 --> 00:05:38.043
Are you serious?

00:05:39.054 --> 00:05:42.260
- This is actually the
tiktok, same tiktok idea

00:05:42.260 --> 00:05:43.610
that he made me film,

00:05:43.610 --> 00:05:46.130
but I never sent him and
I'm still sitting on it.

00:05:46.130 --> 00:05:47.220
God, I shouldn't be saying this.

00:05:47.220 --> 00:05:48.190
They're going to watch this.

00:05:48.190 --> 00:05:49.830
Like sometimes, you know

00:05:49.830 --> 00:05:51.790
if my teachers are teaching a lesson

00:05:51.790 --> 00:05:54.130
and I already know the
lesson, or I just don't feel

00:05:54.130 --> 00:05:55.940
like paying attention, I will mute them.

00:05:55.940 --> 00:05:57.780
I'll, I'll put the computer on mute.

00:05:57.780 --> 00:05:59.370
And it's a little scary because what

00:05:59.370 --> 00:06:00.500
if they call your name?

00:06:00.500 --> 00:06:02.420
In real life it's harder to mute someone.

00:06:02.420 --> 00:06:04.630
The old fashioned way
is just falling asleep.

00:06:04.630 --> 00:06:06.753
- I, I seen the button in the classroom.

00:06:06.753 --> 00:06:09.950
I've seen it on the table and
I'm very tempted to take it.

00:06:09.950 --> 00:06:13.500
That button on zoom,
oh my, that end button

00:06:13.500 --> 00:06:14.540
or like leave button.

00:06:14.540 --> 00:06:18.620
So tempting, sometimes who
like I like hover around it

00:06:18.620 --> 00:06:19.453
in class.

00:06:19.453 --> 00:06:21.200
Like I'll like, I'm like,
I'm going to touch it

00:06:21.200 --> 00:06:22.700
but I'm not going to touch it.

00:06:26.028 --> 00:06:28.183
I think he's told us this before.

00:06:29.770 --> 00:06:32.653
I'm pretty sure America is
going to be at the bottom.

00:06:35.620 --> 00:06:38.670
- Teachers. I feel like
are super underpaid.

00:06:38.670 --> 00:06:41.206
Some kids spend most of their
day with their teachers.

00:06:41.206 --> 00:06:43.170
And you know, if you
have sports and stuff,

00:06:43.170 --> 00:06:45.790
that's coaches too, who
are usually also teachers.

00:06:45.790 --> 00:06:47.220
When we were actually going to school

00:06:47.220 --> 00:06:48.176
like you go to your,

00:06:48.176 --> 00:06:51.670
you go to school and you're
there for like six, eight hours.

00:06:51.670 --> 00:06:53.500
You go home, you're home
alone for a little bit.

00:06:53.500 --> 00:06:54.690
Your parents get home late.

00:06:54.690 --> 00:06:57.000
You're with your teacher more
than your parents sometimes.

00:06:57.000 --> 00:06:57.833
And you know,

00:06:57.833 --> 00:07:00.870
I feel like they're just not
appreciated enough in society.

00:07:00.870 --> 00:07:03.290
People don't give them as
much credit as they deserve.

00:07:03.290 --> 00:07:04.830
Like, I can name you like a bunch

00:07:04.830 --> 00:07:07.120
of good teachers I've
had that have just like

00:07:07.120 --> 00:07:09.900
changed my life and made
me the person I am today.

00:07:09.900 --> 00:07:10.733
We love teachers.

00:07:10.733 --> 00:07:13.150
- That's the one thing I
really started appreciating

00:07:13.150 --> 00:07:15.644
during COVID and virtual
and hybrid learning.

00:07:15.644 --> 00:07:19.066
Like teachers really do so much
and they sacrifice so much.

00:07:19.066 --> 00:07:22.250
And like they're essentially
essential workers.

00:07:22.250 --> 00:07:24.110
So we should like treating them like that.

00:07:24.110 --> 00:07:26.730
- I know some teachers
who have like second jobs

00:07:26.730 --> 00:07:29.060
and it's, it's, I'm not gonna, you know,

00:07:29.060 --> 00:07:30.370
I'm not going to call them sad

00:07:30.370 --> 00:07:33.940
or anything, but like a lot of
teachers put in way more work

00:07:33.940 --> 00:07:36.005
than they need to just to
make sure they're the best

00:07:36.005 --> 00:07:37.070
that they can be.

00:07:37.070 --> 00:07:41.770
And it's just sad to see
like such a important

00:07:41.770 --> 00:07:45.870
job be so undervalued
and so unappreciated.

00:07:45.870 --> 00:07:48.040
- And a lot of teachers,
most of my teachers

00:07:48.040 --> 00:07:50.030
not even just only Feronni, a lot

00:07:50.030 --> 00:07:52.130
of my teachers have gotten
me through this year.

00:07:52.130 --> 00:07:53.553
So, you know,

00:07:53.553 --> 00:07:55.709
even when you feel a little bummy,

00:07:55.709 --> 00:07:58.810
fix that hair, comb
your hair a little bit,

00:07:58.810 --> 00:08:00.360
take off the hoodie, you know

00:08:00.360 --> 00:08:02.860
get out of bed, like at
least like show your face

00:08:02.860 --> 00:08:05.510
or answer a question in
class, for like five minutes

00:08:05.510 --> 00:08:08.860
or just one moment so
that you can tell you too

00:08:08.860 --> 00:08:11.438
like 'I'm listening, I'm there for you.'

00:08:11.438 --> 00:08:12.271
You know.

00:08:12.271 --> 00:08:13.920
- If you're a teacher
watching this, get tiktok

00:08:13.920 --> 00:08:15.890
if you're not on it, you
know, it's a funny thing.

00:08:15.890 --> 00:08:16.723
It's wholesome.

00:08:16.723 --> 00:08:18.260
Cause it just shows like, you know,

00:08:18.260 --> 00:08:20.890
they're down to try to
connect with their students

00:08:20.890 --> 00:08:22.855
and show how they really are and be funny.

00:08:22.855 --> 00:08:25.438
(upbeat music)

